{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979584-2e-not-enough-spell-factors-summoning-scelesti-problem","id":979584,"title":"[2E] Not enough Spell Factors? Summoning Scelesti problem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-01T04:22:43-07:00","id":979584,"title":"[2E] Not enough Spell Factors? Summoning Scelesti problem","content":"So I want to run to final my Yellow Sign subplot. Players are gone to confront Scelesti cultists in Free Council cabal. One of them is Master of Prime, Gnosis 7 character. I think to myself - 'Hell, they are Scelesti, it's final of story line - Let's go big and it want to summon Real Big Bad Abyssal, Rank 5.' I do quick math and it need 8 Paradox Reach. 'Oh, she will get it, she has Gnosis 7' I think to myself. I do next math and this would mean like she need to have Paradox Dice Pool of 24 ( taking statistical 1/3 of Dice Pool as success ). Okay, checking her Paradox Dices per Reach ( on Gnosis Table ) I see she get them 4 per each over Reach. As casting 4th level Prime <i>Celestial Fire</i>, it reads she will need to spend 8 Reach options on spell. I literally used all Advanced and this spell options and I'm <i>still</i> one Reach short. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I will just run the scene as it is, but from mechanical stand point, even badass Scelesti cannot summon anything. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T04:51:39-07:00","id":979594,"title":"","content":"It's Scelesti, right? And the Scelesti <i>wants</i> to summon an Abyssal?<br /> <br /> If the Scelesti knows the players are coming and has time to prepare, maybe try using the Summon Supernal Entities rules but have the mage summon an Abyssal instead.<br /> <br /> If you want it to be an accident due to spell, the best you can really do is just hand-wave that the Scelesti failed badly enough.<br /> <br /> Some ways to get more Paradox dice:<br /> <br /> Cast a lot of Paradox-inducing spells in a row (+1 per spell)<br /> Be Inured to the spell you're casting (+2 every time you cast the spell, even if it wouldn't provoke Paradox otherwise)<br /> Cast in public (+1, but a bigger crowd also gives 9-again, 8-again, or even Rote)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T04:57:25-07:00","id":979596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979584-2e-not-enough-spell-factors-summoning-scelesti-problem?p=979594#post979594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's Scelesti, right? And the Scelesti <i>wants</i> to summon an Abyssal?<br /> <br /> If the Scelesti knows the players are coming and has time to prepare, maybe try using the Summon Supernal Entities rules but have the mage summon an Abyssal instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, she <i>want </i>to summon being. Also, I thought that powerful character ( 5th dot in Prime, Gnosis 7 ) should work easier just to cast spell AND summon being in the same turn than doing proper Abyssal Summoning. She is going to control her Paradox Reaches on to Summon Reach.<br /> <br /> Inured on <i>Celestial Fire</i> and casting previous Paradox inducing spells have sense, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T06:28:55-07:00","id":979622,"title":"","content":"Don't forget you can also make up things to spend Reach on. That's basically what the Reach clauses are all about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T20:44:46-07:00","id":980038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979584-2e-not-enough-spell-factors-summoning-scelesti-problem?p=979596#post979596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inured on <i>Celestial Fire</i> and casting previous Paradox inducing spells have sense, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a decent number of Sleepers on hand likewise can't hurt her chances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:14:56-07:00","id":980093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979584-2e-not-enough-spell-factors-summoning-scelesti-problem?p=980038#post980038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a decent number of Sleepers on hand likewise can't hurt her chances.</div> </div> </div> </div>It will also hinder attacking Pentacle forces, so it's a plus. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T09:34:52-07:00","id":982742,"title":"","content":"Also worth mentioning, rank 5 is a demi-god sort of thing with terrible powers and dicepools. You don't have to go quite that far in order to show them a 'terrible boss' unless the players themselves are demi-god-esque.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T09:41:07-07:00","id":982746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979584-2e-not-enough-spell-factors-summoning-scelesti-problem?p=982742#post982742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also worth mentioning, rank 5 is a demi-god sort of thing with terrible powers and dicepools. You don't have to go quite that far in order to show them a 'terrible boss' unless the players themselves are demi-god-esque.</div> </div> </div> </div>My PCs are Gnosis 5&amp;6 Double Adepts and Masters - they surely are in demi-god-esque regions. They even beat other form of this Abyssal being two sessions before. But hey, as possible Hieromagus, they need to 'fight Abyss'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T10:46:00-07:00","id":982789,"title":"","content":"Ok, to be more detailed, a rank 5 gets 36 to 45 attribute dots, spread out over three attributes and they roll two of those attributes together when taking actions. Their dicepools are going to be in the 20 to 30 range for most things, higher for a few. These things even PUNCHING you will often lead to serious injuries and other consequences, and that's before we consider their ability to spend essence, use numina and influence.<br /> A blast numen for such a being could easily do 8 lethal in a turn, if they're _bad_ at it.<br /> <br /> It's your game though, and it certainly sounds like your players ARE kinda badass, but honestly I'm thinking that either the issue might be white-room reasoning for the fight or it's terribleness isn't being appropriately played out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:30:54-07:00","id":982892,"title":"","content":"I don't think Wyrd is whiterooming, he's using this in a game he's actually running, and his players have taken down entities of this magnitude before. Whether or not he's utilizing these entities' capabilities to their full potential I don't know, but it doesn't much matter - his actual play experience has been that the players are able to deal with these kinds of threats pretty consistently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:47:35-07:00","id":982905,"title":"","content":"It IS very demanding on PCs - but not 'just killing' mages on players group with backup. They <i>can </i>take care of it, barely, but can. I just see a bit hole in Scelasti summoning rules if slightly more experienced groups of NPCs has problem to summon this things with most potent magic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:52:36-07:00","id":982907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979584-2e-not-enough-spell-factors-summoning-scelesti-problem?p=982905#post982905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I just see a bit hole in Scelasti summoning rules if slightly more experienced groups of NPCs has problem to summon this things with most potent magic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>But... there are no merits or systems for scelesti in corebook besides hint on controlling paradox with gnosis . Just make them.<br /> Something like exchange one mana for paradox die or &quot;empty&quot; +1 reach. They would literally rip open reality by pomping mana in till it breaks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 10-06-2016, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T02:48:45-07:00","id":983231,"title":"","content":"I'd say Scelestus are always under the Abyssal Imago Condition. They should be able to use &quot;empty&quot; Reach just to pump up Paradox pools, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> suggested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T04:02:54-07:00","id":983241,"title":"","content":"It's quite a trick to find a &quot;hole&quot; in the rules for Nasnasi Scelesti replacing their ability to summon Supernal entities for one that summons Gulmoth, given that I haven't published them yet.<br /> <br /> Do you have any other critiques of material we haven't written? It would save a lot of time on upcoming projects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T06:44:06-07:00","id":983287,"title":"","content":"Make it a combined spell with an arcanum she doesn't have that many dots in.<br /> <br /> There you go, all the over-reach you could possibly need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T07:56:39-07:00","id":983324,"title":"","content":"Sounds like he wasn't even aware you were going to release rules like that, Dave.<br /> <br /> Not that hard to do that in the meantime as a stop-gap, either, Wyrd; just use the Supernal Summoning rules and invert the success modifiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T09:20:41-07:00","id":983360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979584-2e-not-enough-spell-factors-summoning-scelesti-problem?p=983241#post983241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's quite a trick to find a &quot;hole&quot; in the rules for Nasnasi Scelesti replacing their ability to summon Supernal entities for one that summons Gulmoth, given that I haven't published them yet.<br /> <br /> Do you have any other critiques of material we haven't written? It would save a lot of time on upcoming projects.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Dave</b>, I did not have any ill intentions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I just forgotten you said rules from <b>Left Hand Path</b> will be updated to 2E in blog post ( or similar way ), so this is why this topic. Any possibility of having those in near future?<br /> <br /> Still, I need to have some working stop-gap for next week session. <b>For now, I think that spending Mana for <i>adding</i> Paradox dices is elegant and working solution to Nasnasi ways.</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-07-2016, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}